# A pattern containing a slash is anchored to the directory holding this file.
# `ios/Pods/` therefore matched <root>/ios/Pods, which does not exist — the real
# path is app/ios/Pods. Patterns below are written without a leading path so
# they match at any depth.
#
# This is a public repository. Everything here is either build output, machine
# state, or something that must never leave a developer's laptop. When adding a
# rule, say which of the three it is.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and signing material. Never commit these.
#
# Losing a signing key means losing the ability to update the app; publishing
# one means anyone can ship an update that users' phones will accept as ours.
# See docs/RELEASE.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.jks
*.keystore
key.properties
*.p12
*.pem
*.cer
*.p8
*.certSigningRequest
*.mobileprovision
*.provisionprofile
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets.properties
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output and machine state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Dart / Flutter
.dart_tool/
build/
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
.pub-cache/
.pub/
coverage/
doc/api/
.fvm/
# A contributor pointing a dependency at a local checkout writes this file. It
# is correct for their machine and wrong for everybody else's.
pubspec_overrides.yaml

# The lockfile is committed. This is an application, not a library: a build that
# cannot be reproduced from the tree is not a build anyone can audit, and the
# cryptography here is the reason that matters.
!pubspec.lock

# Android
.gradle/
.kotlin/
.cxx/
local.properties
captures/

# iOS / macOS
Pods/
.symlinks/
ephemeral/
Flutter.framework/
Flutter.podspec
*.xcuserstate
*.xcscmblueprint
xcuserdata/
DerivedData/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors, OS, and scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Backup and merge leftovers. `project.pbxproj.bak` was sitting in the tree and
# would have been committed on the first push — a second, older copy of the
# Xcode project, which is exactly the file someone opens by mistake.
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*~
*.swp
*.swo

# IDE
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.idea/
.vscode/

# OS
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Per-developer tool scratch does not belong here. This file is shared, so a
# rule in it announces which tools everyone is expected to run. Put personal
# ignores in .git/info/exclude, which is local to your clone.
